foundation.question_text:
The network diagram represents streets for travel between Home ($A$) and School ($D$), with numbers indicating travel times in minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (2.4,3.2);
\coordinate (C) at (2.4,1.2);
\coordinate (D) at (4.8,1.2);
\coordinate (E) at (2.4,-0.4);
\coordinate (F) at (0,0.4);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$3$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$4$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above] {$7$};
\draw (A) -- (F) node[midway, left] {$4$};
\draw (F) -- (E) node[midway, below] {$3$};
\draw (E) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (E) -- (D) node[midway, below right] {$6$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the travel time in minutes along the path $A\text{–}F\text{–}E\text{–}D$.

Refer to the Home-to-School street network:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (2.4,3.2);
\coordinate (C) at (2.4,1.2);
\coordinate (D) at (4.8,1.2);
\coordinate (E) at (2.4,-0.4);
\coordinate (F) at (0,0.4);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$3$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$4$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$5$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, above] {$7$};
\draw (A) -- (F) node[midway, left] {$4$};
\draw (F) -- (E) node[midway, below] {$3$};
\draw (E) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$2$};
\draw (E) -- (D) node[midway, below right] {$6$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$E$};
\fill (F) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Compare the two routes $A\text{–}B\text{–}C\text{–}D$ and $A\text{–}C\text{–}E\text{–}D$. Which route is faster, and by how many minutes?

The diagram shows the daily passenger flights leaving Brisbane ($B$) to Sydney ($S$), Melbourne ($M$), and Cairns ($C$).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (B) at (1.5,1.5);
\coordinate (C) at (1.5,3.2);
\coordinate (S) at (3.5,0.5);
\coordinate (M) at (0.2,0);
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$8$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (S) node[midway, above right] {$22$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (M) node[midway, above left] {$16$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$C$};
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$S$};
\fill (M) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the total number of daily flights departing from Brisbane.

development.question_text:
The weighted graph shows walking times between five lookouts $D, A, B, E, C$ in minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (D) at (0,1.2);
\coordinate (A) at (1.8,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3.8,2.4);
\coordinate (E) at (5.2,1.2);
\coordinate (C) at (2.6,0);
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$18$};
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$x$};
\draw (B) -- (E) node[midway, above right] {$23$};
\draw (D) -- (C) node[midway, below left] {$14$};
\draw (C) -- (E) node[midway, below right] {$26$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$12$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$15$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$D$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$E$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
If it takes $59\text{ minutes}$ to walk the path $D\text{–}A\text{–}B\text{–}E$, solve for the value of $x$.

A directed road system connects Start ($S$) to Destination ($T$):
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,1.2);
\coordinate (A) at (2.2,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (2.2,0.2);
\coordinate (T) at (4.5,1.2);
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (A) node[midway, above left] {$8$};
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (B) node[midway, below left] {$6$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B) node[midway, right] {$3$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (T) node[midway, above right] {$12$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (T) node[midway, below right] {$10$};
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$S$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$B$};
\fill (T) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
List all valid directed paths from $S$ to $T$ and identify the longest path.
